# Original fictional investigation packet, not execution against the real product.
Feature: Investigate an upload defect using versioned requirements and observations

  Scenario: REAL-TECH-001 — Select the applicable requirement before judging a report
    Given an obsolete size rule, its explicit replacement and a vague support message
    When the learner writes expected behavior for the current candidate
    Then the expectation cites the current rule and exact byte boundary
    And unknown report details remain questions rather than invented reproduction facts

  Scenario: REAL-TECH-002 — Bound a finding to the observed attempt
    Given a valid under-limit PNG blocked in the UI, a successful control and an interrupted over-limit attempt
    When the learner classifies the supplied records
    Then the UI mismatch is identified on its recorded build and fixture
    And the passing control contradicts a claim that every upload fails
    And the interrupted attempt remains unconfirmed despite its expected rejection

  Scenario: REAL-TECH-003 — Write a useful reproduction and discriminating test plan
    Given observed behavior and a possible stale client limit
    When the learner prepares an investigation
    Then it names fixture type and bytes, environment, steps, expected and actual behavior
    And it plans matched browser and direct-service checks plus below, at and above boundary cases
    And new test rows remain not run and the suspected cause stays a hypothesis

  Scenario: REAL-TECH-004 — Revise the plan when requirements and proposed code change
    Given a retained initial investigation and a later requirement admitting JPEG
    When a proposed client patch is described without verification
    Then the revised plan adds JPEG expectations for the new candidate prospectively
    And prior observations retain their original builds and expectations
    And no proposed fix or unexecuted plan is presented as verified

  Scenario: REAL-TECH-005 — Keep the learner's investigation and revision recoverable
    Given the initial and revised investigations use separately identified evidence
    When the learner opens supplied comparisons and explicitly saves the notebook
    Then both versions and their reason remain unchanged by the comparison
    And the download includes the complete source packet
    And editing clears the applicable self-check while older notebooks remain separate
